IMPORT prelude

-- Building and Construction Authority Act 1999 (Singapore) -- Part 7, the supply of essential construction materials (granite,
-- sand and gazetted materials): what counts (s 27), the import licence and the per-consignment import permit (ss 28, 29), isolation
-- of imported consignments until tested (ss 30, 36), licence eligibility and permit lifetimes (ss 31, 32, 34, 35), failed material
-- (s 38), revocation and appeals (ss 40, 42), the unlicensed-import carve-outs (s 46), and from Part 8 the composition ceiling
-- (s 52) and the right to refuse an officer who will not identify himself or herself (s 50(4)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/BCAA1999.txt (SSO "Current
-- version as at 01 Oct 2026"), with amendments to Act 15 of 2026 (wef 1 July 2026) shown; s 29 carries Act 25 of 2021 (wef
-- 1 April 2022).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 4 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. Most of the Act establishes and runs the
-- Authority (Parts 2 to 6); the decision content an ordinary business meets is in Part 7. SCOPED accordingly. Not encoded: the
-- Authority's constitution, functions, staff, finance and transfer provisions (Parts 2 to 6), s 13 protection from liability,
-- licence conditions procedure (s 33), authorised analysts and certificate evidence (s 39), search and seizure powers (s 43) beyond
-- the penalty table, forfeiture (s 44), the register (s 45), service of documents (s 54) and every regulation.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Building and Construction Authority Act 1999 -- essential construction materials`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS
    IF `a` LESS THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `27 -- what is essential construction material, and what is an import`

-- s 27: "essential construction material" means any of the following "which are suitable for use in any building works, street
-- works or railway works in Singapore and the domestic supply of which is short": (a) granite; (b) sand; (c) such rocks, minerals
-- or other materials "as the Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, declare". "sand" means sand or gravel suitable as fine
-- aggregate "but excludes any unwashed or unprocessed marine-dredged sand or gravel".
-- "import" means to bring into Singapore from outside, "but does not include" material "to be taken out of Singapore on the same
-- conveyance on which it was brought into Singapore without any landing or transhipment within Singapore".
DECLARE Material IS ONE OF
    `granite blocks`
    `granite aggregate`
    `washed sand`
    `unwashed marine-dredged sand`
    `a gazetted material`
    `an ungazetted material`

GIVEN `the material` IS A Material, `suitable and in short domestic supply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the material is essential construction material` IF
    `suitable and in short domestic supply`
    AND CONSIDER `the material`
        WHEN `unwashed marine-dredged sand` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `an ungazetted material` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `brought from outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `leaves on the same conveyance` IS A BOOLEAN, `landed or transhipped` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an import` IF
    `brought from outside Singapore` AND NOT (`leaves on the same conveyance` AND (NOT `landed or transhipped`))

§§ `28 and 46 -- the import licence`

-- s 28(1): "a person must not carry on any business of importing any essential construction material unless the person is
-- authorised to do so under a valid licence". (2): $500,000 or 2 years or both, and $10,000 "for every day or part of a day" the
-- offence continues after conviction. (3): a corporation or LLP whose licence has ceased may carry on "any activity necessary to the
-- winding up". s 46(2): nothing in Part 7 prevents an unlicensed person importing "worked monumental granite, granite sculptures or
-- statues" or millstones, grindstones and granite grinding wheels.
GIVEN `carries on a business of importing it` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a valid licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `only winding up after the licence ceased` IS A BOOLEAN, `monumental granite or millstones` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `importing without a licence is an offence` IF
        `carries on a business of importing it`
    AND (NOT `holds a valid licence`)
    AND (NOT `only winding up after the licence ceased`)
    AND (NOT `monumental granite or millstones`)

GIVEN `days the offence continues after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 28 maximum fine` MEANS
    500000 PLUS 10000 TIMES `days the offence continues after conviction`

§§ `29 -- an import permit for every consignment`

-- s 29(1): a licensee must not import unless (a) "each consignment" is authorised by an import permit and carried out in accordance
-- with its conditions and (b) "the whole consignment conforms to the description in the import permit". (2): $500,000 or 2 years.
-- (3): a defence "for the accused to prove" (a) the offence was due to another person's act or default or a cause beyond control
-- AND (b) "all reasonable precautions" and "all due diligence". (4): if the defence blames another person, not without the court's
-- permission unless written notice identifying that person was served on the prosecutor "7 clear days before the hearing".
GIVEN `due to another person or a cause beyond control` IS A BOOLEAN, `blames another person` IS A BOOLEAN, `took all reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN, `clear days notice before the hearing` IS A NUMBER, `court permits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 29 defence is available` IF
        `due to another person or a cause beyond control`
    AND `took all reasonable precautions`
    AND (    (NOT `blames another person`)
         OR  `clear days notice before the hearing` AT LEAST 7
         OR  `court permits`)

GIVEN `imported by a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN, `permit covers the consignment` IS A BOOLEAN, `permit conditions kept` IS A BOOLEAN, `whole consignment conforms` IS A BOOLEAN, `defence proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 29 offence is made out` IF
        `imported by a licensee`
    AND (    (NOT `permit covers the consignment`)
         OR  (NOT `permit conditions kept`)
         OR  (NOT `whole consignment conforms`))
    AND (NOT `defence proved`)

§§ `30 and 36 -- isolation until tested`

-- s 36(2): every consignment imported "(whether or not under an import permit)" is "deemed subject to an isolation order until the
-- Authority lifts the isolation order in accordance with section 38". (3): the Authority or an enforcement officer may, "before the
-- entry into Singapore", by written notice waive (2). (1): the Authority may in any case issue an isolation order on entry.
-- s 30(1): while a consignment is under an isolation order the licensee must not use it in building, street or railway works, or
-- supply it knowing or having reasonable cause to believe it is for such works. (3): $40,000 or 12 months, $1,000 a day continuing.
GIVEN `waived before entry` IS A BOOLEAN, `order issued on entry` IS A BOOLEAN, `lifted by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consignment is under an isolation order` IF
    (`order issued on entry` OR (NOT `waived before entry`)) AND (NOT `lifted by the Authority`)

GIVEN `under an isolation order` IS A BOOLEAN, `used in works` IS A BOOLEAN, `supplied knowing it is for works` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using or supplying it is an s 30 offence` IF
    `under an isolation order` AND (`used in works` OR `supplied knowing it is for works`)

§§ `31, 34 and 35 -- how long a grant lasts`

-- s 31(5): a licence is valid for the period specified "(being not longer than 5 years)" [Act 15 of 2026 wef 01/07/2026].
-- s 34(6): an import permit "(being not longer than 14 days)" and may be extended.
-- s 35(5): a storage permit "(being not longer than 3 months)", extendable before expiry.
DECLARE Grant IS ONE OF
    `a licence`
    `an import permit`
    `a storage permit`

GIVEN `the grant` IS A Grant, `years` IS A NUMBER, `months` IS A NUMBER, `days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the specified validity is within the limit` IF
    CONSIDER `the grant`
    WHEN `a licence` THEN `years` LESS THAN 5 OR (`years` EQUALS 5 AND `months` EQUALS 0 AND `days` EQUALS 0)
    WHEN `an import permit` THEN `years` EQUALS 0 AND `months` EQUALS 0 AND `days` AT MOST 14
    WHEN `a storage permit` THEN `years` EQUALS 0 AND (`months` LESS THAN 3 OR (`months` EQUALS 3 AND `days` EQUALS 0))

§§ `32 -- who may be licensed`

-- s 32(1): eligible "if, and only if" (a) "the person is not a company limited by guarantee or a corporation sole"; (b) the Authority
-- is satisfied the person is duly authorised to carry on the business of an importer; and (c) the person provides a procurement plan
-- stating (i) the types of material, (ii) the sites, (iii) the methods, (iv) the risks of disruption, and (v) a plan of action.
-- Eligibility is not entitlement: s 31(3) leaves the grant to the Authority, and s 32(3) lets it refuse an applicant who cannot show
-- sufficient material and financial resources.
DECLARE Applicant IS ONE OF
    `a company limited by shares`
    `a company limited by guarantee`
    `a corporation sole`
    `a limited liability partnership`
    `an individual trader`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS A Applicant, `duly authorised to import` IS A BOOLEAN, `procurement plan has all five items` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant is eligible for a licence` IF
        `duly authorised to import`
    AND `procurement plan has all five items`
    AND CONSIDER `the applicant`
        WHEN `a company limited by guarantee` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a corporation sole` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 34(5): "Despite subsection (4), the Authority must refuse to grant an import permit to any licensee whose licence is suspended or
-- who is the subject of any proceedings under section 40."
GIVEN `licence suspended` IS A BOOLEAN, `subject of s 40 proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority must refuse the import permit` IF
    `licence suspended` OR `subject of s 40 proceedings`

§§ `38 -- failed material and who must be told`

-- s 38(5): where the failed material was a sample taken at any time under s 36(6) (rather than the entry sample under s 36(4)), the
-- licensee must, besides removing or destroying it under (4), notify "every person to whom the licensee has supplied essential
-- construction material between the day the consignment of failed construction material enters into Singapore and the seventh day
-- after the Authority receives the authorised analyst's certificate relating to that consignment (both days inclusive)".
-- Days are counted here as day numbers on one calendar.
GIVEN `sample taken under s 36(6)` IS A BOOLEAN, `day supplied` IS A NUMBER, `day of entry` IS A NUMBER, `day certificate received` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the customer must be notified` IF
        `sample taken under s 36(6)`
    AND `day supplied` AT LEAST `day of entry`
    AND `day supplied` AT MOST `day certificate received` PLUS 7

§§ `40 -- revocation, suspension and penalties`

-- s 40(1): the Authority may revoke if satisfied that (a) a s 33 condition was breached; (b) the licence was obtained by fraud or
-- misrepresentation; (c) bankruptcy or liquidation "other than for the purpose of amalgamation or reconstruction"; (d) conviction of
-- an offence under Part 7; (e) failure without reasonable excuse to comply with s 38(4) or (5); (f) "the public interest or national
-- security of Singapore so requires"; (g) failure to comply with a s 40(2)(b) or (d) order.
-- (2): if no cause "of sufficient gravity for revoking": suspension up to 6 months, a financial penalty up to $500,000, censure, or
-- directions.
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `breach of a licence condition`
    `licence obtained by fraud`
    `liquidation for amalgamation`
    `compulsory liquidation`
    `conviction under Part 7`
    `conviction under another Act`
    `failed-material duties ignored`
    `national security`
    `a late annual return`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ground permits revocation` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `liquidation for amalgamation` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `conviction under another Act` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a late annual return` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 40(3): no order under (1) or (2) unless the licensee had an opportunity to be heard "being a period of at least 7 and not more
-- than 14 days".
GIVEN `days given to be heard` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the hearing period is lawful` IF
    `days given to be heard` AT LEAST 7 AND `days given to be heard` AT MOST 14

-- s 40(5): an order "takes effect on the expiry of 7 days after" service. (6): but a financial penalty under (2)(b) that has been
-- appealed under s 42 "does not take effect unless the order is confirmed by the Minister or the appeal is for any reason dismissed
-- by the Minister or withdrawn". Only the financial penalty is held back by an appeal; revocation and suspension are not.
GIVEN `days since service` IS A NUMBER, `is a financial penalty` IS A BOOLEAN, `appealed` IS A BOOLEAN, `appeal confirmed, dismissed or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order has taken effect` IF
        `days since service` AT LEAST 7
    AND (    (NOT `is a financial penalty`)
         OR  (NOT `appealed`)
         OR  `appeal confirmed, dismissed or withdrawn`)

-- s 40(7)(c): on revocation the importer "is debarred from applying for or holding a licence for a period of 12 months after that
-- revocation". The text does not say whether the 12th month is inside or outside the bar; month 12 is not tested.
GIVEN `months since revocation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the former licensee may apply again` IF
    `months since revocation` AT LEAST 12

§§ `42 -- appeal to the Minister`

-- s 42(1)-(3): refusals, conditions, s 40 orders and permit cancellations may be appealed to the Minister "within 14 days" after
-- notification or service, "whose decision is final".
GIVEN `days since notified` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF
    `days since notified` AT MOST 14

§§ `Penalty table and s 52 composition`

-- Maximum fines read from the deposit: s 28(2) and s 29(2) $500,000; s 30(3) $40,000; s 31(6), 34(8), 35(6) false applications
-- $20,000; s 36(5) failing to isolate $10,000; s 39(4) false analyst $20,000; s 43(8) failing to give information $10,000; s 48(2)
-- the Authority's symbol $10,000; s 49(1) grants obtained by false statements $25,000; s 50(1) obstruction $20,000.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `unlicensed import`
    `import without a permit`
    `using isolated material`
    `false licence application`
    `failing to isolate`
    `posing as an authorised analyst`
    `withholding information from an officer`
    `misusing the Authority's symbol`
    `obtaining a grant by false statement`
    `obstructing an officer`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unlicensed import` THEN 500000
    WHEN `import without a permit` THEN 500000
    WHEN `using isolated material` THEN 40000
    WHEN `false licence application` THEN 20000
    WHEN `failing to isolate` THEN 10000
    WHEN `posing as an authorised analyst` THEN 20000
    WHEN `withholding information from an officer` THEN 10000
    WHEN `misusing the Authority's symbol` THEN 10000
    WHEN `obtaining a grant by false statement` THEN 25000
    WHEN `obstructing an officer` THEN 20000

-- s 52(1): an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" may be compounded for "a sum not exceeding the lower of" (a) "one half
-- of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence" and (b) "$5,000". Which offences are compoundable is left to
-- regulations not retrieved; this computes only the ceiling.
GIVEN `maximum fine for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition ceiling` MEANS
    `the smaller of` (`maximum fine for the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000

§§ `50(4) -- refusing an officer who will not identify himself or herself`

-- s 50(3): every police, customs or immigration officer, enforcement officer and assisting officer must, "if not in uniform, declare
-- his or her office" and on demand produce an identification card. (4): "It is not an offence" to refuse (a) a police, customs or
-- immigration officer "not in uniform who fails to declare his or her office and refuses to produce his or her identification card
-- on demand"; or (b) an enforcement or assisting officer "who fails to declare his or her office and refuses to produce" the card.
-- Reading: (4)(b) has no "not in uniform" words, so for an enforcement or assisting officer the uniform is taken not to matter.
DECLARE Officer IS ONE OF
    `a police officer`
    `an officer of customs`
    `an enforcement officer`
    `an assisting officer`

GIVEN `the officer` IS A Officer, `in uniform` IS A BOOLEAN, `declared office` IS A BOOLEAN, `produced card on demand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refusing the officer is not an offence` IF
        (NOT `declared office`)
    AND (NOT `produced card on demand`)
    AND CONSIDER `the officer`
        WHEN `a police officer` THEN NOT `in uniform`
        WHEN `an officer of customs` THEN NOT `in uniform`
        OTHERWISE TRUE
